Focus Feed Next — preserve every MP4 variant

Upstream keeps only the highest-bitrate MP4 and discards the rest, so a
consumer cannot offer a quality choice at all: by the time the JSON is written,
the alternatives are gone.

Three surgical changes, all additive:

  models.py         TweetMedia gains `variants`, `poster_url`, `duration_ms`,
                    each defaulted, so every existing construction still works.
  parser.py         Fills them from `video_info`, which already has everything
                    needed — no extra request, no new field from X.
  serialization.py  Emits them, and reads them back, only when present.

The existing `url` field keeps its exact previous meaning — the highest-bitrate
MP4 — so an unpatched consumer sees no change at all.

Resolution comes from the variant URL path (`.../1280x720/...`), which is how X
encodes it; it is parsed defensively and left absent rather than guessed.
`duration_ms` and `poster_url` are emitted only when X genuinely sent them.

--- a/twitter_cli/models.py
+++ b/twitter_cli/models.py
@@
 class TweetMedia:
     type: str  # "photo" | "video" | "animated_gif"
     url: str
     width: Optional[int] = None
     height: Optional[int] = None
+    # Focus Feed Next: every playable MP4, not only the largest.
+    variants: List["MediaVariant"] = field(default_factory=list)
+    poster_url: Optional[str] = None
+    duration_ms: Optional[int] = None
+
+
+@dataclass
+class MediaVariant:
+    """One playable rendition of a video."""
+
+    url: str
+    content_type: str
+    bitrate: Optional[int] = None
+    width: Optional[int] = None
+    height: Optional[int] = None

